# Repo-root .dockerignore for the agent-runtime-base image build.
# Build context is the repo root (Dockerfile lives in runtime-image/ but COPYs
# from cli/ — see runtime-image/Dockerfile and .github/workflows/runtime-image.yml).
#
# Docker does NOT honor .gitignore — anything below mirrors gitignore entries
# that could otherwise leak into the build context (and to remote buildx
# builders). Codex pass 6 of slice 4.2 caught the original missing entries.

# Editor / tooling state
**/.obsidian/
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/
**/excalidraw.log

# Node ecosystem cruft (the npm-installed adapter ships from the registry,
# not from local node_modules; nothing in the image build needs these).
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/.npm/
**/*.log
**/coverage/
**/.nyc_output/

# Go build outputs (the image builds agentctl from cli/ source inside its
# own buildx Go stage; the local cli/bin/agentctl checkin artifact must NOT
# slip into the build context).
/cli/bin/
**/go-build/

# OS scratch
**/.DS_Store

# Local-only runtime state from running an agent against this repo. These
# can contain session IDs, MCP socket paths, and audit log entries that
# should never leak to a remote builder.
**/.agent-controller/
**/.pi/
**/audit.log

# Private working notes (gitignored; never goes into images)
docs/superpowers/
docs/source-memo/

# Git internals + history
.git/
.gitignore

# Top-level docs / build outputs not needed inside the image
dist/
e2e/
docs/
scripts/

# Other workflows + project files not needed for the image build
.github/
SECURITY.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
CHANGELOG.md
ROADMAP.md
README.md
LICENSE
